{"id":"stamps-get-a-face","parent":"opqp8gbi","ord":"a0","title":"A node's created/changed stamps get a face in the UI","todo":true,"desc":"The stamps exist (props-floor) and the search grammar reads them (#257: created:/changed:), but no surface SHOWS them — you can query by a stamp you can never see. Give them a face where a reader looks: the node drawer/detail at least; possibly a quiet row affordance (hover, or beside the ¶). Honesty caveat to design around: a node written before the stamps carries none (absence is not a past), and the 2026-08-21 roadmap reorg re-captured old nodes so their created is the re-capture time, not the filing time — the face should not present a stamp as older provenance than it is; true history is git log.","created":"2026-08-21T14:37:33-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 — 'I have hard time figuring out when these were created. Shouldn't this be a feature?'"}}
{"id":"9idc4xwp","parent":"g7ej78wl","ord":"a3","title":"Documents & markdown"}
{"id":"fm-authored-record","parent":"9idc4xwp","ord":"a0","title":"Frontmatter as the document's own fields #deferral #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- #302 made frontmatter keys searchable properties (prop:/has:). The remaining half: reading them as record fields — a date: drawn on the day page, agenda and calendar; a done: as a mark; edges.\n- Refused in #302 because a frontmatter date that search selects but no page draws would split the grammar — all three date surfaces read Node/Dated.\n- An arc, not a line. Also named in brainstorming/first-class-documents.md, frontmatter.ts, docs/format.md and docs/search.md.\n- Also refused there: tags: values as face tags, and nested/block YAML.","created":"2026-08-20T19:53:41-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T14:45:40-04:00","custom":{"from":"#302"}}
{"id":"fwpdlpyl","parent":"g7ej78wl","ord":"a4","title":"Upstream (kolu)"}
{"id":"changed-frame-tax-upstream","parent":"fwpdlpyl","ord":"a0","title":"Upstream: changed()'s per-frame cost belongs in kolu #deferral #kolu-upstream","todo":true,"desc":"- Four kolu follow-ups from #299 (the reactivity finale), each ruled deferrable by its review:\n  - Registering on changed()/arrayKey drops the tracker into whole-frame comparisons; the cheaper spine-walk shape belongs upstream.\n  - The keyed merge leaves the tracker holding a second full copy of every frame.\n  - The per-member schema guard answers a question every kolu app has; kolu's own guard doesn't check it.\n  - Batched deltas delivery can't honour a key, so key declarations buy nothing there.\n- Kolu-repo work — needs the human's ratification before filing.","created":"2026-08-20T18:14:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T14:45:40-04:00","custom":{"from":"#299"}}
{"id":"hv3ch4yw","parent":"g7ej78wl","ord":"a5","title":"Navigation, panes & layout"}
{"id":"landing-open-questions","parent":"hv3ch4yw","ord":"a0","title":"Landing: is one history entry per write on a previewed page livable? #deferral #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- #319 closed three of the four landing questions with one rule: a landing's geometry may only correct an act still in flight, and flight ends when the reader moves the frame or the 2s window runs out; each pane lands its own.\n- What remains: a revision bump on a previewed .html still costs ONE history entry (down from three).\n- Getting to zero means loading a second iframe behind the first and swapping on load — doubles the frame's state machine and changes what's on screen during the fetch. Ruled expensive at #319.\n- Wants the human's ruling: live with one entry per write, or pay for the doubled machine.\n\n**pr** — closed Q2/Q3/Q4; Q1 remains","created":"2026-08-21T07:41:57-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T14:37:33-04:00","custom":{"from":"#305","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/1d640926","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/319"}}
{"id":"klvv5cgn","parent":"ty6mbbm6","ord":"a6","title":"Git & sync"}
{"id":"team-multi-writer","parent":"klvv5cgn","ord":"a0","title":"Team hosting: several people writing on one branch #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- The human plans to host olai as a team notebook with coworkers invited.\n- #301 only guarantees the auto loop can't corrupt: it never forces, never retries, never auto-pulls; a refused push stops with git's words on screen.\n- Multi-writer needs real answers: fetch, a merge policy, whose-work-is-whose in the UI, and where rebase-before-push fits (deliberately not automated today — a conflicted rebase is a conversation, not a state the auto loop may enter).","created":"2026-08-20T19:59:12-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T14:45:40-04:00","custom":{"from":"#301","reclassified":"the human 2026-08-21 — not a deferral but a new feature request; moved deferred.olai → features.olai/Git & sync, #deferral dropped; from=#301 kept as provenance of where the idea surfaced"}}
