{"id":"instructions-md-breakdown","parent":"5t0tm7em","ord":"a2","title":"instructions.md graduates into the orchestrator's outline data, step by step","todo":true,"desc":"The ruling (2026-08-25): stage-shaped rules live on dag.olai's step nodes — each step's desc is that stage's law, read when it applies, carried into every lane. The plan doc holds the full inventory (every instructions.md section → its destination), the dag drift catalogue (opencode step, clone-vs-mirror law, empty CI step, pre-typed prop names), the target kernel (~10 lines), and the beat order: CI law first, then deferrals, merge/retire, reviews, implement, board protocol, kernel rewrite last. One graduation per beat; the doc's covered lines die only after their node lands — a rule is never owned twice.","created":"2026-08-25T15:37:14-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/instructions-breakdown.md","from":"the human 2026-08-25, planning with the orchestrator after agent-model-pin's cancellation raised the where-do-rules-live question"}}
