{"id":"td-close","parent":"vwl2alm8","ord":"a0","title":"folds + CI once (the orchestrator's) + the HUMAN rules; merge order: #2216 first, re-pin, then this","doing":true,"desc":"MORNING PLAN (the human, 2026-08-26): the author resolves the PR's conflicts (the night's #404/#406 landed on master), then the human DEPLOYS #405 UNMERGED to production for a live test — the real padi, the real fleet, this vault's own lanes as the corpus (the one thing the fake-padi suite couldn't exercise). The orchestrator frame-verifies live as the evidence gate: dot states cross-checked against kolu ls, the hollow face (padi briefly stopped if the human allows), the snapshot pane + refetch, the one-connection claim across tabs. Divergence from the fake → back to the author pre-merge; clean → the human's merge word. CI re-runs at the conflict-resolved head before merge (the re-verdict rule). Prior state: both reviews folded, kolu#2216 merged (35732510), re-pin literal, CI was green 11/11 at 9170398f. Open besides the merge: the UUID-face display question; the p0 body's two judgment calls.","after":["td-review-grok","td-review-pi"],"created":"2026-08-25T18:55:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T09:13:05-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"cb9dcd13"}}
{"id":"padi-status-header","parent":"5n5m4p3q","ord":"a1","title":"The padi connection's status joins the header bar beside \"live\"","doing":true,"desc":"The header already tells the connection truth for the vault (\"live\", \"committed · 1m ago\"); the padi link deserves the same chrome — connected / absent / contract-skew as a small indicator beside \"live\", drawing from the same `cells.kolu` the dots consume (a second reader of the existing cell — no new wire). The rationale from the live test: a per-chip hollow face is ambiguous (unknown terminal? dead mirror?), and the reader shouldn't diagnose app health from whichever dot is on screen. Skew's \"upgrade one of these\" sentence is exactly a header-grade message. Natural follow-up to #405; small.","created":"2026-08-26T09:15:15-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T10:41:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-26, during #405's live test — a hollow dot made them ask whether the MIRROR was dead, and nothing app-level answered","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/405"}}
